    <p class="govuk-body">
      On 15 January 2026, Percival Snodgrass acted as lookout while co-defendant Tabitha Quibble selected and concealed three items worth £247.50 at Selfridges — an AllSaints dress (£99.49), an AllSaints handbag (£124.99), and a Lululemon yoga mat (£23.02). As both defendants approached the exit, security guard Millicent Bumble moved to intercept them. Snodgrass pushed Bumble forcefully, causing her to fall and sustain shoulder and arm injuries requiring medical treatment. Both defendants fled and were apprehended within 15 minutes.
    </p>
